#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Climate TRACE as columns, the view row rearranged, and OpenStreetMap detail
on the outlines with relief and building heights.

- View row: Globe / Flat map, then zoom in and out one above the other, then
  "Snap back to global scale" over "Leave Earth". The compass sits under the
  3D terrain tick box, left of the notes on how to tilt.
- Climate TRACE: every source in the loaded tiles stands as a column, height
  by the square root of its emissions, in its subsector's colour, rebuilt when
  the map stops moving. Click a column for its figures.
- Country outlines: the CARTO layer that asked for an API key is gone.
  OpenStreetMap from OpenFreeMap (free, no key) is drawn in the map's own
  muted darks: relief shading, water, woods, towns, rivers, roads and rail,
  and from zoom 13 buildings raised to their mapped heights.
- News wires: the footnote is gone. "Who reports it" stays, with "News
  source" (the outlet) under it.

Needs patch_wires_marks.py first.
Run from the repo root:  python3 patch_columns_osm.py
"""
import pathlib
import sys

